  "text_sanskrit": "अश्रद्दधानाः पुरुषा धर्मस्यास्य परन्तप । अप्राप्य मां निवर्तन्ते मृत्युसंसारवर्त्मनि ॥ ९-३ ॥",
  "itrans": "ashraddadhAnAH puruShA dharmasyAsya parantapa . aprApya mA.n nivartante mR^ityusa.nsAravartmani .. 9-3 ..",
  "translation": "Those that are without faith in this knowledge relating to Dharma (the supporter, the Lord), O slayer of foes, do not come to Me and only remain fixed in the path of birth and death. (3)\nV. Without faith: having no belief that the knowledge inculcated here surely leads to the achievement of the highest purpose of man.\nA. By the term Pratyukshâvagama the direct realisation of Brahma is referred to. And by the term Dharmaya the true knowledge of the Lord by means of the Sâstras is conveyed. The latter is the step leading to the former. It is this knowledge that has been promised and extolled. The neglect of it has been condemned. This has been divided into Gnana and Vignana. Of these Gnana is expounded here below. (4 to 15)",
